{"id":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-codazzi-harmonic-tensor","title":"def:pet-ch9-codazzi-harmonic-tensor","path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.md","line":331,"body":"","kind":"definition","status":"not_started","tex":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex#def:pet-ch9-codazzi-harmonic-tensor","uses":["[[references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique#def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/Petersen/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_TheBochnerTechnique.tex","label":"def:pet-ch9-codazzi-harmonic-tensor","line":717,"source":"\\begin{definition}[Codazzi and harmonic symmetric tensors]\n  \\label{def:pet-ch9-codazzi-harmonic-tensor}\n\n  \\source{petersen:page-0364}\n  \\uses{def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative}\n  Call a symmetric tensor $h$ \\emph{Codazzi} when $d^\\nabla h=0$; call it\n  \\emph{harmonic} when it is Codazzi and also divergence free,\n  $\\nabla^*h=0$.\n\\end{definition}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Definition</div></section>[Codazzi and harmonic symmetric tensors] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6465663a7065742d6368392d636f64617a7a692d6861726d6f6e69632d74656e736f72\"></span> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source\" style=\"display:block\">Source: <span class=\"reference\">petersen:page-0364</span></span> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FPetersen%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_TheBochnerTechnique%23def%3Apet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative\">↗ def:pet-ch9-codazzi-exterior-derivative</a> Call a symmetric tensor <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$h$\">$h$</span> <em>Codazzi</em> when <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$d^\\nabla h=0$\">$d^\\nabla h=0$</span>; call it <em>harmonic</em> when it